WEBVTT

00:02.480 --> 00:04.022
Water.

00:04.816 --> 00:06.316
Earth.

00:07.026 --> 00:08.360
Fire.

00:09.028 --> 00:10.279
Air.

00:11.155 --> 00:14.992
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.285 --> 00:19.162
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.706 --> 00:22.624
Only the Avatar,
master of all four elements,

00:22.709 --> 00:23.709
could stop them.

00:23.793 --> 00:25.294
But when the world needed him most,

00:25.378 --> 00:26.878
he vanished.

00:27.422 --> 00:29.339
100 years passed, and my brother and I

00:29.424 --> 00:32.592
discovered the new Avatar,
an airbender named Aang.

00:32.885 --> 00:34.761
And although his airbending
skills are great,

00:34.846 --> 00:37.723
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

00:37.807 --> 00:39.016
Unh!

00:39.100 --> 00:42.060
But I believe Aang can save the world.

01:01.956 --> 01:08.587
Unh!

01:18.306 --> 01:19.306
Where's Momo?

01:23.895 --> 01:24.978
Hang on, Momo!

01:39.285 --> 01:40.827
All right, you too.

01:41.704 --> 01:43.163
This is going to take forever.

01:46.584 --> 01:47.709
That works.

01:52.590 --> 01:53.590
These are Fire Nation traps.

01:54.092 --> 01:55.634
You can tell from the metalwork.

01:55.718 --> 01:57.594
We'd better pack up camp
and get moving.

01:59.597 --> 02:01.681
No flying this time.

02:01.766 --> 02:03.558
What? Why wouldn't we fly?

02:03.643 --> 02:04.768
Think about it.

02:04.852 --> 02:07.229
Somehow Prince Zuko
and the Fire Nation keep finding us.

02:07.563 --> 02:09.981
It's because they spot Appa,
he's just too noticeable.

02:10.066 --> 02:12.442
What? Appa's not too noticeable.

02:12.568 --> 02:15.278
He's a gigantic fluffy monster
with an arrow on his head!

02:15.405 --> 02:16.530
It's kind of hard to miss him.

02:18.324 --> 02:20.450
Sokka's just jealous
because he doesn't have an arrow.

02:20.785 --> 02:21.952
I know you all want to fly,

02:22.036 --> 02:23.120
but my instincts tell me

02:23.204 --> 02:24.871
we should play it safe
this time and walk.

02:25.164 --> 02:26.623
Who made you the boss?

02:26.707 --> 02:28.291
I'm not the boss, I'm the leader.

02:28.626 --> 02:30.627
You're the leader?

02:30.711 --> 02:32.671
But your voice still cracks.

02:32.755 --> 02:34.714
I'm the oldest, and I'm a warrior!

02:34.799 --> 02:36.591
So I'm the leader.

02:36.676 --> 02:38.510
If anyone's the leader, it's Aang.

02:38.719 --> 02:40.470
I mean, he is the Avatar.

02:40.680 --> 02:42.639
Are you kidding?
He's just a goofy kid.

02:43.808 --> 02:44.933
He's right.

02:45.435 --> 02:47.853
Why do boys always think
someone has to be the leader?

02:48.521 --> 02:50.856
I bet you wouldn't be so bossy
if you kissed a girl.

02:51.149 --> 02:52.357
I've kissed a girl!

02:52.442 --> 02:53.567
You just haven't met her.

02:53.651 --> 02:55.777
Who? Gran-Gran?

02:55.862 --> 02:57.320
I've met Gran-Gran.

02:57.405 --> 02:58.822
No, besides Gran-Gran.

02:58.906 --> 03:00.949
Look, my instincts tell me

03:01.033 --> 03:02.784
we have a better chance
of slipping through on foot,

03:02.869 --> 03:04.619
and a leader has to
trust his instincts.

03:04.704 --> 03:08.123
Ok, we'll try it your way,
O wise leader.

03:08.332 --> 03:10.041
Who knows? Walking might be fun.

03:11.210 --> 03:12.544
Walking stinks!

03:12.920 --> 03:15.130
How did people go anywhere
without a flying bison?

03:15.214 --> 03:16.673
I don't know, Aang.

03:16.757 --> 03:18.383
Why don't you ask Sokka's instincts?

03:18.593 --> 03:20.385
They seem to know everything.

03:20.595 --> 03:21.928
Ha ha, very funny.

03:22.138 --> 03:24.055
I'm tired of carrying this pack.

03:24.140 --> 03:26.558
You know who you should
ask to carry it for a while?

03:26.767 --> 03:28.018
Sokka's instincts!

03:28.227 --> 03:29.769
That's a great idea.

03:30.188 --> 03:31.980
Hey, Sokka's instincts,
would you mind--

03:32.064 --> 03:33.773
Ok, ok, I get it!

03:33.858 --> 03:35.525
Look, guys, I'm tired, too.

03:35.610 --> 03:38.612
But the important thing is that
we're safe from the Fire Nation.

03:43.826 --> 03:44.826
Run!

03:49.332 --> 03:50.332
We're cut off!

03:50.416 --> 03:51.583
Sokka, your shirt!

03:51.667 --> 03:52.667
Aah!

04:00.718 --> 04:03.261
If you let us pass,
we promise not to hurt you.

04:03.721 --> 04:04.971
What are you doing?

04:05.056 --> 04:06.389
Bluffing.

04:06.766 --> 04:08.850
You, promise not to hurt us?

04:08.935 --> 04:09.935
Unh.

04:12.188 --> 04:14.564
Nice work, Sokka. How did you do that?

04:14.649 --> 04:16.441
Instinct?

04:16.859 --> 04:17.859
Look!

04:28.204 --> 04:29.204
Unh!

04:29.830 --> 04:30.914
Down you go.

04:36.963 --> 04:38.463
They're in the trees!

04:38.548 --> 04:39.548
Ha ha ha!

04:54.772 --> 04:57.232
Hah!

04:57.316 --> 04:58.316
Unh!

04:58.401 --> 04:59.526
Hey, he was mine.

04:59.944 --> 05:01.278
Gotta be quicker next time.

05:09.370 --> 05:10.704
Unh!

05:22.300 --> 05:23.300
Man!

05:32.852 --> 05:34.019
Hey.

05:34.103 --> 05:35.103
Hi.

05:39.150 --> 05:41.318
You just took out a whole army
almost single-handed.

05:41.402 --> 05:42.736
Army?!

05:42.820 --> 05:45.030
There were only, like, 20 guys.

05:45.698 --> 05:46.865
My name is Jet,

05:46.949 --> 05:48.199
and these are my freedom fighters.

05:48.618 --> 05:51.870
Sneers, Longshot, Smellerbee,

05:52.288 --> 05:53.997
The Duke, and Pipsqueak.

05:54.624 --> 05:56.708
Pipsqueak, that's a funny name.

05:58.961 --> 06:01.212
You think my name is funny?

06:01.547 --> 06:02.964
It's hilarious!

06:07.678 --> 06:08.678
Unh!

06:20.524 --> 06:23.276
Um, thanks for saving us, Jet.

06:23.611 --> 06:24.819
We're lucky you were there.

06:24.904 --> 06:26.529
I should be thanking you.

06:26.822 --> 06:29.032
We were waiting to ambush
those soldiers all morning.

06:29.367 --> 06:30.700
We just needed the right distraction.

06:30.785 --> 06:32.369
And then you guys stumbled in.

06:32.453 --> 06:34.496
We were relying on instincts.

06:34.789 --> 06:36.331
You'll get yourself
killed doing that.

06:41.462 --> 06:44.547
Hey, Jet, these barrels are filled
with blasting jelly.

06:44.632 --> 06:46.091
That's a great score.

06:46.425 --> 06:48.968
And these boxes are filled
with jellied candy.

06:49.303 --> 06:50.720
Also good.

06:50.805 --> 06:52.055
Let's not get those mixed up.

06:52.390 --> 06:53.848
We'll take the stuff
back to the hideout.

06:54.350 --> 06:55.642
You guys have a hideout?

06:56.018 --> 06:57.018
You want to see it?

06:57.103 --> 06:58.103
Yes, we want to see it!

07:02.191 --> 07:03.274
We're here.

07:03.484 --> 07:04.984
Where? There's nothing here.

07:05.236 --> 07:06.236
Hold this.

07:06.320 --> 07:07.529
Why? What's this do?

07:07.780 --> 07:09.489
Aah!

07:09.573 --> 07:10.615
Aang?

07:10.700 --> 07:11.866
I'll get up on my own.

07:15.996 --> 07:17.330
Grab hold of me, Katara.

07:31.470 --> 07:32.846
Nice place you got!

07:39.270 --> 07:40.645
It's beautiful up here.

07:40.730 --> 07:42.856
It's beautiful, and more importantly,

07:42.940 --> 07:44.482
the Fire Nation can't find us.

07:44.567 --> 07:46.234
They would love to find you,

07:46.318 --> 07:47.610
wouldn't they, Jet?

07:47.695 --> 07:49.404
It's not going to happen, Smellerbee.

07:49.697 --> 07:51.531
Why does the Fire Nation
want to find you?

07:51.615 --> 07:52.991
I guess you could say

07:53.075 --> 07:54.576
I've been causing them
a little trouble.

07:54.660 --> 07:56.703
See, they took over a nearby
Earth Kingdom town

07:56.787 --> 07:57.787
a few years back.

07:58.122 --> 07:59.456
We've been ambushing their troops,

07:59.540 --> 08:01.124
cutting off their supply lines,

08:01.208 --> 08:03.585
and doing anything we can
to mess with them.

08:03.961 --> 08:05.420
One day, we'll drive the Fire Nation

08:05.504 --> 08:06.504
out of here for good,

08:06.589 --> 08:07.589
And free that town.

08:07.673 --> 08:09.466
That's so brave.

08:09.550 --> 08:12.302
Yeah, nothing's braver
than a guy in a tree house.

08:12.595 --> 08:14.262
Don't pay any attention to my brother.

08:14.597 --> 08:16.765
No problem. He probably
had a rough day.

08:16.849 --> 08:18.391
So, you all live here?

08:18.476 --> 08:19.476
That's right.

08:19.560 --> 08:20.935
Longshot over there,

08:21.228 --> 08:23.438
His town got burned down
by the Fire Nation.

08:23.647 --> 08:25.565
And we found The Duke
trying to steal our food.

08:26.108 --> 08:27.942
I don't think he ever
really had a home.

08:28.277 --> 08:29.527
What about you?

08:31.405 --> 08:32.989
The Fire Nation killed my parents.

08:33.741 --> 08:35.575
I was only eight years old.

08:35.951 --> 08:37.660
That day changed me forever.

08:37.745 --> 08:40.663
Sokka and I lost our mother
to the Fire Nation.

08:40.873 --> 08:42.749
I'm so sorry, Katara.

08:53.260 --> 08:55.637
Today, we struck another blow

08:55.721 --> 08:57.055
against the Fire Nation swine.

09:00.893 --> 09:03.812
I got a special joy
from the look on one soldier's face,

09:03.896 --> 09:05.355
when The Duke dropped down
on his helmet

09:05.439 --> 09:07.899
and rode him like a wild hog-monkey!

09:13.030 --> 09:15.281
Now, the Fire Nation
thinks they don't have to worry

09:15.366 --> 09:17.742
about a couple of kids
hiding in the trees.

09:18.202 --> 09:19.702
Maybe they're right.

09:23.791 --> 09:27.252
Or maybe, they're dead wrong.

09:32.132 --> 09:33.925
Hey, Jet, nice speech.

09:34.009 --> 09:35.176
Thanks.

09:35.678 --> 09:36.678
By the way,

09:36.762 --> 09:38.137
I was really impressed
with you and Aang.

09:38.222 --> 09:40.181
That was some great bending
I saw out there today.

09:40.266 --> 09:43.059
Well, he's great. He's the Avatar.

09:43.561 --> 09:44.853
I could use some more training.

09:45.312 --> 09:48.106
Avatar, huh? Very nice.

09:48.482 --> 09:49.607
Thanks, Jet.

09:50.025 --> 09:51.025
So I might know a way

09:51.110 --> 09:52.527
that you and Aang
can help in our struggle.

09:52.611 --> 09:54.863
Unfortunately,
we have to leave tonight.

09:55.614 --> 09:56.948
Sokka, you're kidding me.

09:57.032 --> 09:59.576
I needed you on an important
mission tomorrow.

10:00.077 --> 10:01.077
What mission?

10:15.301 --> 10:16.593
What are you doing?

10:16.677 --> 10:18.595
Shh. It amplifies vibrations.

10:18.679 --> 10:19.846
Good trick.

10:20.472 --> 10:22.015
Nothing yet.

10:22.349 --> 10:23.391
Wait, yes!

10:23.475 --> 10:24.475
Someone's approaching.

10:24.560 --> 10:25.643
How many?

10:25.728 --> 10:26.895
I think there's just one.

10:29.064 --> 10:30.857
Good work, Sokka. Ready your weapon.

10:35.821 --> 10:37.155
Wait! False alarm.

10:37.239 --> 10:38.448
He's just an old man.

10:43.871 --> 10:45.705
What are you doing
in our woods, you leech?

10:45.789 --> 10:48.583
Please, sir, I'm just a traveler.

10:51.754 --> 10:53.171
Unh!

10:58.677 --> 11:00.011
Do you like destroying towns?

11:00.095 --> 11:01.638
Do you like destroying families?

11:01.722 --> 11:03.222
Do you?!

11:03.307 --> 11:06.768
Please, let me go. Have mercy.

11:07.102 --> 11:08.853
Does the Fire Nation let people go?

11:08.938 --> 11:10.605
Does the Fire Nation have mercy?

11:12.858 --> 11:14.275
Jet, he's just an old man!

11:14.360 --> 11:15.985
He's Fire Nation! Search him!

11:16.070 --> 11:17.904
But he's not hurting anyone.

11:17.988 --> 11:20.365
Have you forgotten that
the Fire Nation killed your mother?

11:20.449 --> 11:22.116
Remember why you fight!

11:22.201 --> 11:23.743
We got his stuff, Jet.

11:23.827 --> 11:25.620
This doesn't feel right.

11:25.704 --> 11:28.039
It's what has to be done.
Now let's get out of here.

11:32.836 --> 11:33.836
Come on, Sokka!

11:38.968 --> 11:41.094
Sokka, look what The Duke gave me.

11:48.477 --> 11:50.019
Quit it!

11:50.688 --> 11:52.480
Hey, Sokka. Is Jet back?

11:52.856 --> 11:54.565
Yeah, he's back. But we're leaving.

11:54.650 --> 11:55.733
What?

11:55.818 --> 11:57.527
But I made him this hat.

11:58.320 --> 11:59.988
Your boyfriend Jet's a thug.

12:00.072 --> 12:01.072
What?!

12:01.156 --> 12:02.365
No, he's not.

12:02.700 --> 12:04.075
He's messed up, Katara.

12:04.159 --> 12:05.284
He's not messed up.

12:05.369 --> 12:07.036
He's just got a different way of life.

12:07.121 --> 12:08.579
A really fun way of life.

12:08.872 --> 12:10.039
He beat and robbed

12:10.124 --> 12:11.290
a harmless old man.

12:12.084 --> 12:14.293
I want to hear
Jet's side of the story.

12:15.212 --> 12:16.754
Sokka, you told them what happened,

12:16.839 --> 12:19.298
but you didn't mention
that the guy was Fire Nation?

12:19.383 --> 12:21.926
No, he conveniently
left that part out.

12:22.386 --> 12:24.220
Fine, but even if he was Fire Nation,

12:24.304 --> 12:25.596
he was a harmless civilian.

12:26.015 --> 12:27.223
He was an assassin, Sokka.

12:30.144 --> 12:32.854
See? There's a compartment
for poison in the knife.

12:32.938 --> 12:34.439
He was sent to eliminate me.

12:34.523 --> 12:36.441
You helped save my life, Sokka.

12:36.775 --> 12:38.401
I knew there was an explanation.

12:38.777 --> 12:40.194
I didn't see any knife.

12:40.654 --> 12:42.071
That's because he was concealing it.

12:42.156 --> 12:43.656
See, Sokka?

12:43.741 --> 12:45.867
I'm sure you just
didn't notice the knife.

12:45.951 --> 12:47.660
There was no knife!

12:47.870 --> 12:49.037
I'm going back to the hut

12:49.121 --> 12:50.455
and packing my things.

12:51.373 --> 12:52.874
Tell me you guys aren't leaving yet.

12:52.958 --> 12:54.417
I really need your help.

12:54.501 --> 12:55.543
What can we do?

12:55.919 --> 12:58.004
The Fire Nation is planning
on burning down our forest.

12:58.422 --> 13:00.339
If you both use waterbending
to fill the reservoir,

13:00.424 --> 13:01.716
we could fight the fires.

13:02.092 --> 13:03.342
But if you leave now,

13:03.427 --> 13:05.053
they'll destroy the whole valley.

13:09.224 --> 13:10.516
We can't leave now

13:10.601 --> 13:12.894
with the Fire Nation
about to burn down a forest!

13:12.978 --> 13:14.395
I'm sorry, Katara.

13:14.730 --> 13:16.481
Jet's very smooth,
but we can't trust him.

13:16.899 --> 13:18.483
You know what I think?

13:18.567 --> 13:21.277
You're jealous that he's a better
warrior and a better leader.

13:21.612 --> 13:23.529
Katara, I'm not jealous of Jet.

13:23.614 --> 13:24.739
It's just that my instincts--

13:24.823 --> 13:26.407
Well, my instincts tell me

13:26.492 --> 13:28.576
we need to stay here a little longer
and help Jet.

13:29.078 --> 13:30.244
Come on, Aang.

13:30.662 --> 13:31.662
Sorry, Sokka.

13:41.965 --> 13:42.965
Let's go.

14:05.656 --> 14:06.781
Now listen.

14:06.865 --> 14:08.991
You're not to blow the dam
until I give the signal.

14:09.076 --> 14:10.785
If the reservoir isn't full,

14:10.869 --> 14:12.662
the Fire Nation troops could survive.

14:13.330 --> 14:15.123
But what about the people in the town?

14:15.207 --> 14:17.041
Won't they get wiped out, too?

14:17.251 --> 14:18.793
Look, Duke, that's the price

14:18.877 --> 14:20.878
of ridding this area
of the Fire Nation.

14:21.213 --> 14:22.755
Now don't blow the dam
until I give the signal.

14:22.840 --> 14:23.840
Got it?

14:28.595 --> 14:31.264
Where do you think
you're going, ponytail?

14:36.603 --> 14:37.687
Sokka.

14:37.771 --> 14:39.939
I'm glad you decided to join us.

14:40.941 --> 14:43.526
I heard your plan
to destroy the Earth Kingdom town.

14:43.610 --> 14:46.028
Our plan is to rid the valley
of the Fire Nation.

14:46.113 --> 14:47.822
There are people living there, Jet,

14:47.906 --> 14:49.657
mothers and fathers and children.

14:50.117 --> 14:52.743
We can't win without
making some sacrifices.

14:52.828 --> 14:55.121
You lied to Aang and Katara
about the forest fire.

14:55.372 --> 14:57.456
Because they don't understand
the demands of war.

14:57.541 --> 14:58.958
Not like you and I do.

14:59.168 --> 15:00.501
I do understand.

15:00.586 --> 15:02.086
I understand that
there's nothing you won't do

15:02.171 --> 15:03.337
to get what you want.

15:03.922 --> 15:06.132
I was hoping you'd have an open mind.

15:06.216 --> 15:08.092
But I can see you've made your choice.

15:10.053 --> 15:12.013
I can't let you warn Katara and Aang.

15:12.097 --> 15:13.347
Take him for a walk.

15:13.557 --> 15:14.682
A long walk.

15:14.892 --> 15:16.517
You can't do this!

15:16.602 --> 15:17.935
Cheer up, Sokka.

15:18.228 --> 15:19.687
We're going to win a great victory

15:19.771 --> 15:20.897
against the Fire Nation today.

15:24.151 --> 15:26.903
Jet, I'm sorry about how
Sokka's been acting.

15:26.987 --> 15:29.363
No worries. He already apologized.

15:29.573 --> 15:31.949
Really? Sokka apologized?

15:32.326 --> 15:33.910
Yeah, I was surprised, too.

15:34.578 --> 15:35.703
I got the sense that maybe you

15:35.787 --> 15:36.787
Talked to him or something.

15:36.872 --> 15:37.997
Yeah, I did.

15:38.081 --> 15:39.749
I guess something you said
got through to him.

15:40.125 --> 15:42.084
Anyhow, he went out
on a scouting mission

15:42.169 --> 15:43.794
with Pipsqueak and Smellerbee.

15:43.879 --> 15:44.962
I'm glad he cooled off.

15:45.297 --> 15:47.006
He's so stubborn sometimes.

15:49.051 --> 15:50.301
All right, we're here.

15:50.719 --> 15:52.595
Underground water's trying
to escape from these vents.

15:53.096 --> 15:54.680
I need you guys to help it along.

15:54.973 --> 15:57.767
I've never used bending
on water I can't see.

15:57.851 --> 15:59.227
I don't know...

15:59.436 --> 16:01.896
Katara, you can do this.

16:02.105 --> 16:03.397
What about me?

16:03.607 --> 16:05.566
I know the Avatar can do this.

16:27.089 --> 16:28.756
Yes! Good job.

16:29.007 --> 16:30.591
This river empties into the reservoir.

16:30.676 --> 16:32.385
A few more geysers
and it will be full.

16:33.053 --> 16:35.054
Look, there's another steam vent.

16:36.139 --> 16:37.890
Ok, you two keep it up,

16:37.975 --> 16:39.475
I'll go check on things
at the reservoir.

16:41.186 --> 16:42.979
When we're done,
we'll meet you over there.

16:43.063 --> 16:45.189
Actually, probably better
if you meet me

16:45.274 --> 16:46.565
back at the hideout when you're done.

16:57.077 --> 16:58.536
I bet that's enough.

16:58.620 --> 17:00.079
And I'm not just
saying that to be lazy.

17:00.455 --> 17:02.206
Let's catch up with Jet
at the reservoir.

17:02.582 --> 17:04.542
I thought we agreed
to meet Jet back at the hideout.

17:04.626 --> 17:06.168
Well, we finished early.

17:06.586 --> 17:07.920
I'm sure he'll be happy to see us.

17:11.133 --> 17:13.175
Come on, move along!

17:13.260 --> 17:14.802
How can you stand by and do nothing

17:14.886 --> 17:16.721
while Jet wipes out a whole town?

17:17.055 --> 17:19.348
Hey, listen, Sokka,
Jet's a great leader.

17:19.433 --> 17:23.102
We follow what he says,
and things always turn out ok.

17:27.733 --> 17:29.358
If that's how Jet leads,

17:29.776 --> 17:30.943
Then he's got a lot to learn!

17:31.028 --> 17:32.028
Hey!

17:34.031 --> 17:35.031
Unh!

17:36.325 --> 17:37.533
While you two are up there,

17:37.617 --> 17:39.702
you might want to practice
your knot work.

17:40.579 --> 17:42.163
Hey, Smellerbee.

17:42.247 --> 17:44.165
You going to eat your lychee nuts?

17:44.249 --> 17:45.374
Ooh.

17:52.549 --> 17:53.632
What are they doing?

17:53.717 --> 17:55.092
Hey, those are the red barrels

17:55.177 --> 17:56.344
he got from the Fire Nation.

17:56.595 --> 17:58.387
Why would they need blasting jelly?

17:58.972 --> 18:01.057
Because Jet's going to
blow up the dam.

18:01.475 --> 18:02.475
What?

18:02.559 --> 18:04.352
No, that would destroy the town.

18:04.436 --> 18:06.020
Jet wouldn't do that.

18:06.104 --> 18:07.646
I've got to stop him!

18:08.148 --> 18:09.440
Jet wouldn't do that.

18:09.941 --> 18:10.983
Unh!

18:12.611 --> 18:13.652
Yes, I would.

18:13.737 --> 18:14.987
Jet, why?

18:15.072 --> 18:17.615
Katara, you would, too,
if you just stop to think.

18:18.283 --> 18:20.910
Think about what the Fire Nation
did to your mother.

18:20.994 --> 18:23.537
We can't let them do that
to anyone else ever again.

18:23.830 --> 18:25.539
This isn't the answer.

18:25.624 --> 18:27.792
I want you to understand me, Katara.

18:28.210 --> 18:30.336
I thought your brother
would understand, but--

18:30.712 --> 18:32.254
Where's Sokka?

18:32.339 --> 18:33.339
Katara.

18:36.134 --> 18:37.426
Unh!

18:40.180 --> 18:41.305
I need to get to the dam.

18:43.266 --> 18:45.226
You're not going anywhere
without your glider.

18:45.310 --> 18:46.727
Unh! Uhh! Unh!

18:48.855 --> 18:50.272
I'm not going to fight you, Jet.

18:50.357 --> 18:52.233
You'll have to
if you want your glider back.

19:01.410 --> 19:02.410
Hah!

19:06.206 --> 19:07.206
Unh!

19:13.672 --> 19:14.755
Hah!

19:28.103 --> 19:29.103
Aah!

19:30.105 --> 19:31.188
Unh!

19:31.273 --> 19:32.273
Aah!

19:54.212 --> 19:55.212
Unh!

20:05.432 --> 20:06.432
Aah!

20:06.516 --> 20:07.516
Unh!

20:14.483 --> 20:15.524
Unh!

20:30.040 --> 20:31.874
Why, Jet?

20:31.958 --> 20:34.210
I can't believe I trusted you.

20:34.753 --> 20:36.045
You lied to me!

20:36.129 --> 20:38.088
You're sick, and I trusted you!

20:45.013 --> 20:46.180
What are you doing?

20:46.264 --> 20:47.264
You're too late.

20:47.349 --> 20:48.349
No!

20:51.603 --> 20:52.770
Unh!

20:54.231 --> 20:55.564
Sokka's still out there.

20:55.774 --> 20:57.358
He's our only chance.

20:57.442 --> 20:59.109
Come on, Sokka.

20:59.444 --> 21:01.111
I'm sorry I ever doubted you.

21:01.196 --> 21:02.196
Please...

21:09.788 --> 21:10.871
No.

21:30.600 --> 21:32.184
Sokka didn't make it in time.

21:32.269 --> 21:33.602
All those people.

21:34.604 --> 21:36.146
Jet, you monster!

21:36.231 --> 21:37.856
This was a victory, Katara.

21:37.941 --> 21:39.108
Remember that.

21:39.192 --> 21:40.568
The Fire Nation is gone,

21:40.652 --> 21:41.735
and this valley will be safe.

21:42.070 --> 21:43.445
It will be safe,

21:43.530 --> 21:45.281
without you.

21:46.032 --> 21:47.032
Sokka!

21:47.242 --> 21:48.617
I warned the villagers of your plan,

21:48.702 --> 21:49.702
Just in time.

21:49.786 --> 21:52.121
-What?!
-At first, they didn't believe me.

21:52.205 --> 21:54.790
The Fire Nation soldiers
assumed I was a spy.

21:54.874 --> 21:56.166
But one man vouched for me,

21:56.251 --> 21:58.294
the old man you attacked.

21:58.378 --> 22:01.505
He urged them to trust me,
and we got everyone out in time.

22:06.845 --> 22:08.846
Mrs. Pretty!

22:09.598 --> 22:10.973
Sokka, you fool!

22:11.057 --> 22:12.141
We could have freed this valley!

22:12.225 --> 22:13.392
Who would be free?

22:13.768 --> 22:14.893
Everyone would be dead.

22:15.353 --> 22:16.353
You traitor!

22:16.438 --> 22:18.230
No, Jet. You became the traitor

22:18.315 --> 22:20.190
when you stopped
protecting innocent people.

22:20.609 --> 22:23.110
Katara, please, help me.

22:23.361 --> 22:24.862
Good-bye, Jet.

22:25.530 --> 22:26.822
Yip, yip.

22:31.578 --> 22:33.037
We thought
you were going to the dam.

22:33.371 --> 22:34.872
How come you went to the town instead?

22:34.956 --> 22:36.206
Let me guess.

22:36.291 --> 22:37.875
Your instincts told you.

22:37.959 --> 22:39.460
Hey, sometimes they're right.

22:39.544 --> 22:41.211
Um, Sokka?

22:41.296 --> 22:43.130
You know we're going
the wrong way, right?

22:43.673 --> 22:45.341
And sometimes they're wrong.
